{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1553458-spirit-3-rouse-spirit","id":1553458,"title":"Spirit 3, Rouse Spirit","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-08-26T08:16:13-07:00","id":1553458,"title":"Spirit 3, Rouse Spirit","content":"Hello everyone,<br /> <br /> I am playing an Euthanatoi character, a Vrati that wants to revolutionize the Tradition and move it in its next cycle of existence, essentially pushing for the dissolving of dogma and fiery ritual, for a more subtle and coincidental approach, the type of character not to abide the &quot;once you join the Chakravanti you will only wear black clothes&quot; law, which is a joke in itself but I trust you can see how it translates to the common belief.<br /> <br /> Alas, he is a Vrati, so he does what a Vrati must. Recently, as a Deathwealker, he's learned Spirit 3. For his equipment, he uses a katar and a bow &amp; arrow, granted his Totem (Kali) will give him shit if he uses cowardly ways such as guns.<br /> <br /> The question is, now, if he were to use Spirit 3 to permanently rouse the Spirits within his katar and bow, what sort of benefits would that bring, aside from 2 mouthy Spirits that will not stop complaining if he stumbles?<br /> <br /> I am talking both fluff-wise and mechanically, since every -1 difficulty or +1 die counts.<br /> <br /> Thank you in advance for your ideas and answers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13197-skeeper0","name":"Skeeper0","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-26T10:02:05-07:00","id":1553461,"title":"","content":"Awakened items can exist in several worlds at once, they can be used to attack ephemeral entities in the other side of the gauntlet while remaining on the phisical realm yourself, and don't count for the difficulty of taking stuff there with (not that it was very significant to begin with)<br /> <br /> Awakened objects aren't very talktive and don't have much of a personality to begin with, but they will gain a stronger sentience with time and story, and can hold a strong ressonance<br /> <br /> They can work better in very minnor coincidental ways. An awakened gun can refuse to fire against their owner (so, a bow may break the string if someone else steals it and tries to fire an arrow). An awakened kinfe never looses it's edge. They don't give any permanent bonus, but I think a -1 to diffs using the item for it's intended use it's ok (and I have the impression that was a rule somewhere, but I don't remember where)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-26T11:23:35-07:00","id":1553465,"title":"","content":"With the exception of combat. -1 dif for the intended use, with the exception of combat.<br /> <br /> I think it's in W20 somewhere, but I can't verify now.<br /> <br /> Overall that's it. There are benefits, possibly a lot depending partly on you, partly on the ST. Dealing with things in the Penumbra without much of a hassle is probably the bigger one, though.<br /> <br /> But actual benefits for combat-oriented number-crunching? No, that won't do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-26T14:45:29-07:00","id":1553471,"title":"","content":"So, there is some things to discuss with your ST that matters more than anything else.<br /> <br /> Mostly freshly awakened spirits aren't really capable of much. But if they're permanently roused and cared for, they're going to get stronger. How your ST wants to handle that is going to matter a lot.<br /> <br /> Think of it like buying a puppy to raise as a scent-hound. While magic could expedite various things, it is better to raise the puppy yourself for a number of philosophic and practical reasons (broadly, any magic that makes a dog more loyal, capable of obey your commands, and better at the tasks you train them for will be even better if you're stacking training and magic instead of just using magic). How would that work out in play? Spirits are a bit more complicated that an animal breed for thousands of years to bond with humans and see us as authority figures, but the game logic of what it means to have a puppy you're training into a dog is obviously going to matter how far along the process you are.<br /> <br /> So a freshly awake spirit is kinda like a new puppy, more work than benefit, maybe some small bonuses like monteparnas suggested. How much growth the spirit sees in play is going to matter. The spirits are going to know what matters to your PC regarding what they might see that the mage doesn't. They might get better stats. They might get Charms that let them do more active things. Etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-29T08:26:04-07:00","id":1553537,"title":"","content":"The rote is unclear on this and seems to meander back and forth between if the mage is awakening the spirit to act on its own, or awakening it to perform specific functions. &quot;A powerful shaman can rouse the spirits to perform clearly impossible acts: offering advice, running without fuel, locking out trespassers who try to break into an awakened house, and other sorts of paranormal phenomenon.&quot; <br /> <br /> Then there's the vulgarity. The system text says awakening spirits is normally coincidental but could tip into vulgarity if they are roused to do uncanny things. But vulgarity is typically determined at casting. Its most profound effect is changing the difficulty of casting and how much paradox the mage gets during casting. We don't revisit either of those after the fact. So it doesn't tend to matter systems wise if an effect proves to be unbelievable down the road, except if the optional and hazy rules for Unbelief are involved.<br /> <br /> All of which sounds like the mage has to set at least some of the scope of what awakening an object means when he's awakening the object, which doesn't fully mesh with the descriptive text or what you are going for.<br /> <br /> So this will need to involve a good conversation with your ST to work out systems and expectations.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-29T11:10:29-07:00","id":1553541,"title":"","content":"I personally think the very suggestion of this being Vulgar is very weird.<br /> <br /> Unless you somehow makes the awakening itself Vulgar, why would the actions of the spirit be Vulgar? It's a spirit. Everywhere else in the game, including in the <b>Spirit</b> Sphere, their actions are their own, independent and not beholden to vulgarity or Paradox.<br /> <br /> Not to say there's what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> put, at the end of the day this is about the spirit's capabilities, and freshly awakened spirits just aren't that much. How does this effect alters their initial capabilities? This seems pretty out of context for this effect, and for this level of the Sphere anyway.<br /> <br /> Can you somehow interfere in the spirit's traits? Make it awaken already as a more powerful being? Are you infusing years of experience into their being? That's confusing, it brings more questions than really helps anything at all, except if interpreted as a &quot;do anything&quot; effect that can bypass the entirety of the rest of the Magic system and base results solely on an even more arbitrary number of successes than usual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-29T14:37:08-07:00","id":1553548,"title":"","content":"Well, there's no particular reason why you can't use higher rankings in Spirit to boost(or diminish, or just change) a Spirit like Life/Matter/Mind can do to their purviews.<br /> <br /> I think spirits in WoD cosmology don't really work on &quot;experience&quot; like other beings. Their power (including their knowledge and skill at tasks) is dictated by their nature. A spirit grows in power by having its nature reinforced over and over. How that reinforcement goes matters. A healing spirit that is consistently reinforced as a spirit of medicine might suddenly be able to tap into broad scientific knowledge of medicine without any actual medical training because it's nature is to know these things now. If you just reinforced its nature as a more passive positive regenerative presence it might not know anything about anatomy but got a Charm for mass healing instead.<br /> <br /> I do agree the text of the Sphere is meh, but since we're not constrained to a specific analytical heuristic (no offense to the very good thread about the Spheres, but that sort of deep analysis only goes so far when it comes to figuring out how someone wants to put the game to use), we can pull on more resources to figure out how to handle various issues the effect implies.<br /> <br /> Though, there's also just a temptation to backport the CofD 2e spirit rules since it makes adjudicating what a spirit can do so much easier (CofD 2e spirits have an additional set of powers called Influence that dictate their ability to manipulate material aspects of what they represent rather than the specific powers granted by Charms). Then you can draw a simple line between what a spirit can do that's within their Influence(s) and what would be the mage pushing a spirit beyond such things via magic as a basis for a vulgar/coincidental determination in Ascension.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}